# Python virtualenv

This repo uses **`deployment_env/`**, not `.venv`.

## Activate (Git Bash on Windows)

```bash
# ❌ BAD — .venv does not exist in this project
source .venv/Scripts/activate

# ✅ GOOD
source deployment_env/Scripts/activate
```

## Invoke Python

Prefer the venv interpreter explicitly when not activated:

```bash
# ❌ BAD
.venv/Scripts/python.exe script.py

# ✅ GOOD
deployment_env/Scripts/python.exe script.py
```

When running modules (MCP servers, smoke scripts), activate `deployment_env` first, set `PYTHONPATH=.` from the repo root if needed, then run `python`.
